# CODEOWNERS -- required reviewers per path.
# Anything that can break CI, publish to npm, or change release/versioning
# policy needs @JoShMiQueL's approval before merge. Code in packages/src
# stays unowned so normal changes flow without a review bottleneck.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# CI + release pipeline -- can publish to npm, change the build, or bump deps.
.github/workflows/     @JoShMiQueL
.github/dependabot.yml @JoShMiQueL

# release-please manifest + config -- decides versions, channels, tags.
release-please-config.json   @JoShMiQueL
.release-please-manifest.json   @JoShMiQueL

# Native build config -- the Node-26 thin-LTO workaround lives here;
# a bad edit breaks the .node on modern Node.
**/binding.gyp    @JoShMiQueL

# Package manifests -- deps, publish files, scripts, bin, exports.
**/package.json    @JoShMiQueL

# Release policy doc.
docs/releasing.md    @JoShMiQueL
